    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP is anchored by **Mickey Moniak**, who carries the highest daily efficiency score of 75.98. His matchup against Luinder Avila is the standout play of the slate, benefiting from a massive 14% park factor boost and an equally favorable platoon advantage. Similarly, **James Wood** (67.91) and **Austin Riley** (66.33) offer elite upside, though both carry a 37% rain risk that requires monitoring as first pitch approaches. While **Corbin Carroll** faces a tougher test against Parker Messick, his inherent speed remains a non-negotiable asset for our scarcity-driven strategy, keeping him firmly in the mix despite a score-depressing platoon disadvantage.\n\nThe bench decision that triggered the most internal debate was between **Travis Bazzana** and **Isaac Paredes**. While **Paredes** posted a respectable 45.88, he was ultimately left out due to a brutal matchup against the arm of Jacob deGrom; the 19% SP skill penalty proved too heavy a burden for his base projection to overcome. **Bazzana** narrowly claimed the final UTIL spot with a score of 47.69, edging out the bench options primarily due to his positional flexibility and a significantly more favorable matchup against Kohl Drake. Meanwhile, we continue to manage the roster cautiously, keeping an eye on **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor**, both of whom are projected as marginal plays today while we await official lineup confirmation to ensure their spots in the batting order hold the predicted value.",
